timeline.body:
To correct my comment above - early search termination with `ByteProcessor` would only be possible in case of search for multiple occurrences, and the `processor` should expose (based on it's internal state) the minimum amount of bytes needed to complete the needle. If this amount is larger than the remaining part of the haystack, the search could be terminated.
Not very useful IMHO. This callback based API is not well suited for such optimization.
@franz1981

